@startuml
title Context lifecycle and authority boundaries
skinparam shadowing false
top to bottom direction
actor "Host identity" as identity
actor "Authorized publisher" as publisher
component "Screen + input judge\nshared-document mode" as ingest
database "Shared store\ntenant + explicit readers\nsource + digest + expiry" as shared
database "Session store\ntenant + subject owner\nbounded accepted turns + TTL" as sessions
component "ContextStore.bundle\nauthorize before selection" as bundle
component "HumanMessage(JSON)\nuntrusted data envelope" as data
component "SystemMessage\noperator-owned policy" as system
component "Input judge, selected specialist, output judge" as model
component "Chatbot._commit\nhost-owned memory write" as memory_commit
identity --> sessions : opaque session
publisher --> ingest : bounded text + source + readers
ingest --> shared : checks pass
identity --> bundle : trusted principal
shared --> bundle : tenant AND reader AND unexpired
sessions --> bundle : exact owner check
bundle --> data : whole records within budget
system --> model : instructions
data --> model : evidence
model ..> memory_commit : code accepts output evidence
memory_commit --> sessions : recheck owner; append accepted exchange
note bottom of shared
Source labels are assertions, not verified authenticity.
SHA-256 identifies content, not truth or authorship.
No URL fetching or cross-tenant sharing.
Shared-document inspection requires no specialist route.
end note
note bottom of sessions
Screened exchanges remain untrusted.
Rejected inputs, drafts and judgments are not checkpointed.
/reset deletes a session; TTL cleanup occurs on access.
Process exit clears memory; TTL is not secure erasure.
end note
footer Agentic Drink Book | Policy 2.1.0 | Model judgments remain fallible
@enduml
